            <ArticleTitle>[Coronary artery dissection secondary to coronary arteriography: presentation of two cases and review of the literature].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>567-73</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two reports of coronary artery dissection secondary to coronary arteriography and followed by emergency aorto-coronary bypass are presented. One case includes pathological specimen demonstrating medial and intimal change in the dissected coronary artery, which may have predisposed this artery to dissect. Also the literature on catheter-induced coronary artery dissection is reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
